- `apps/web/lib/db.ts|models.ts|types.ts|redis.ts|rate-limit.ts` — data layer (BP §4–§5): cached Mongoose connection with `strictQuery: 'throw'`, cleared on a failed connect; models and indexes in one file; types in `lib/types.ts` as the single source (Zod at boundaries mirrors them); node-redis, failing closed when `REDIS_URL` is missing; an atomic fixed-window limiter. Local Mongo is a single-node replica set (transactions need one, CP §6.8). Any script that writes data calls `scripts/lib/assert-local-db.ts` first, and runs as `pnpm --filter web script scripts/<name>.ts` (`tsx --conditions=react-server`, BP §14).
